UID:124bce3bc6a0dc2c@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART:20261106T133000Z
DTEND:20261106T143000Z
SUMMARY:US jobs report (October)
DESCRIPTION:October nonfarm payrolls and unemployment rate.\n\nEconomists p
 olled by LSEG expected 65k. A strong print would add to the case for a Dec
 ember Fed hike\, which is bearish for crypto and long-duration tech and su
 pportive for the dollar. Outcome: payrolls rose 165k\, well above the 65k 
 estimate.\n\nBLS Employment Situation schedule: https://www.bls.gov/schedu
 le/news_release/empsit.htm\nFox Business: US economy adds 165\,000 jobs in
  October: https://foxbusiness.com/economy/us-jobs-report-october-2026
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/empsit.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1ff3391996ed63bc@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:US-Ukraine-Russia talks\, Abu Dhabi
DESCRIPTION:First three-way round in about nine months\, focused on securit
 y guarantees.\n\nRussia agreed to resume the three-way talks after Witkoff
  met Putin on October 21. A ceasefire isn't on the agenda\, and Russia rej
 ects any European troops in Ukraine. Strikes on Ukraine's grid and a Russi
 an refinery came hours before the talks. Progress would weigh on oil and l
 ift European cyclicals. A collapse would support oil and gold. Outcome: th
 e talks ended on November 11 without a breakthrough\, and Witkoff and Kush
 ner said they'd fly to Moscow to meet Putin the next day.\n\nKyiv Independ
 ent: envoys to Moscow as Abu Dhabi talks end without breakthrough: https:/
 /kyivindependent.com/2nd-day-of-trilateral-peace-talks-begins-between-ukra
 ine-russia-us-in-abu-dhabi/\nNews On AIR: hostilities continue before US-b
 rokered talks: https://newsonair.gov.in/hostilities-continue-between-russi
 a-and-ukraine-before-scheduled-us-brokered-talks/\nADN: Putin agrees to re
 sume three-way talks: https://www.adn.com/nation-world/2026/10/21/putin-ag
 rees-to-resume-three-way-talks-on-ukraine-war-with-kyiv-and-washington-kre
 mlin-says/
CATEGORIES:geopolitics
URL:https://kyivindependent.com/2nd-day-of-trilateral-peace-talks-begins-be
 tween-ukraine-russia-us-in-abu-dhabi/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e9f8bb7efd634991@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART:20261110T133000Z
DTEND:20261110T143000Z
SUMMARY:US CPI (October)
DESCRIPTION:October consumer prices\, with forecasts of +0.3% headline and 
 +0.2% core month over month.\n\nSeptember headline was +0.6%. Fed Governor
  Waller said core at 0.3% or higher would call for a stronger policy move.
  A hot print lifts yields and the dollar\, which hurts crypto\, tech and g
 old. BLS isn't publishing year-over-year rates because of the 2025 shutdow
 n. Outcome: headline +0.4% and core +0.3%\, both hot. The 2Y rose 17bp to 
 4.74%\, the 10Y neared 5% and CME odds of no December move fell to about 3
 %.\n\nBLS CPI release schedule: https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/
 cpi.htm\nBenzinga: Hot CPI pushes 10-year yield to 5%: https://www.benzing
 a.com/markets/equities/26/11/63117496/stock-market-today-hot-cpi-treasury-
 yields-5-percent-nvidia-slides\nStartup Fortune: December Fed hike now pri
 ced in: https://startupfortune.com/treasury-yields-jump-after-hot-october-
 cpi-with-a-december-fed-hike-now-priced-in/
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/cpi.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:77daac68318d714e@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261113
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:Witkoff and Kushner meet Putin in Moscow
DESCRIPTION:US envoys take the Abu Dhabi results to Putin after the three-w
 ay talks ended without a deal.\n\nThe Abu Dhabi agenda covered a ceasefire
 \, energy and Black Sea security. Ukraine wants a European-led reassurance
  force and Article 5-style guarantees. AP reports neither side has shown w
 illingness to compromise\, and Moscow wants Europe kept out of the direct 
 talks. Movement toward a ceasefire would weigh on oil and lift European cy
 clicals. A breakdown would support oil and gold.\n\nKyiv Independent: envo
 ys to Moscow as Abu Dhabi talks end: https://kyivindependent.com/2nd-day-o
 f-trilateral-peace-talks-begins-between-ukraine-russia-us-in-abu-dhabi/\nK
 yiv Post: second day of Abu Dhabi talks ends: https://www.kyivpost.com/pos
 t/89761
CATEGORIES:geopolitics
URL:https://kyivindependent.com/2nd-day-of-trilateral-peace-talks-begins-be
 tween-ukraine-russia-us-in-abu-dhabi/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1b2afa1d94c8076a@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART:20261117T220000Z
DTEND:20261117T230000Z
SUMMARY:Nvidia Q3 FY2027 earnings
DESCRIPTION:Nvidia reports the quarter ended October 25 after the US close.
  Consensus is about $108.8bn revenue and $2.47 EPS.\n\nThe consensus figur
 es come from MarketBeat via InsiderFinance. The stock goes into the report
  after a sharp one-month drop on the spy-report overhang and talk of tight
 er China export rules. A miss or weak China guidance would extend the semi
 s and AI selloff and drag crypto-linked stocks. A beat could spark a sharp
  rebound in semis and the Nasdaq. On November 11 the WSJ reported the boar
 d was preparing to remove CEO Jensen Huang\, and the shares fell more than
  9% after hours. Reuters said the board met that evening to weigh removal\
 , leave or a reprimand\, with no decision announced. A leadership change b
 efore the report would make the guidance and the call harder to read.\n\nN
 VIDIA: conference call for Q3 results: https://investor.nvidia.com/news/pr
 ess-release-details/2026/NVIDIA-Sets-Conference-Call-for-Third-Quarter-Fin
 ancial-Results/\nReuters via Investing.com: Nvidia board meets on Huang's 
 future: https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/nvidia-is-prepari
 ng-to-oust-ceo-jensen-huang-wsj-reports-5019991\nInsiderFinance: Nvidia ea
 rnings set for Nov. 17: https://www.insiderfinance.io/news/nvidia-earnings
 -set-for-nov-17-amid-sell-signals
CATEGORIES:stocks
URL:https://investor.nvidia.com/news/press-release-details/2026/NVIDIA-Sets
 -Conference-Call-for-Third-Quarter-Financial-Results/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:53be903d3e2dba69@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART:20261125T133000Z
DTEND:20261125T143000Z
SUMMARY:US PCE inflation (October)
DESCRIPTION:The Fed's preferred inflation gauge for October\, the last infl
 ation print before the December FOMC.\n\nOctober CPI was hot at +0.4% head
 line and +0.3% core\, so a firm core PCE is the base case. A hot print rai
 ses the odds of a 50bp December hike\, which would hit crypto\, tech and g
 old. A soft print would ease hike pricing. The date comes from third-party
  calendars\, so check it against the BEA schedule.\n\nBEA: PCE price index
 : https://www.bea.gov/data/personal-consumption-expenditures-price-index\n
 Financecalendar: US PCE report: https://www.financecalendar.com/us-pce-rep
 ort/
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bea.gov/data/personal-consumption-expenditures-price-index
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e1218ed29ec170db@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART:20261204T133000Z
DTEND:20261204T143000Z
SUMMARY:US jobs report (November)
DESCRIPTION:November nonfarm payrolls\, the last labour print before the De
 cember FOMC.\n\nOctober payrolls were 165k against a 65k estimate (LSEG po
 ll). Another strong print would firm up a December hike and raise the odds
  of 50bp\, which is bearish for crypto and tech. A weak print would trim h
 ike pricing and support risk assets and gold.\n\nBLS Employment Situation 
 schedule: https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/empsit.htm
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/empsit.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2629ea169b240101@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART:20261209T190000Z
DTEND:20261209T200000Z
SUMMARY:FOMC rate decision
DESCRIPTION:A 25bp hike from 3.75–4.00% is the market's base case after t
 he hot October CPI.\n\nThe Fed held at its October 28 meeting. Before CPI\
 , Kalshi priced a 25bp hike at 77%. After CPI\, CME FedWatch put the chanc
 e of no move at about 3%\, with economists split between 25 and 50bp. In O
 ctober\, Williams said one more 2026 hike may be appropriate but saw none 
 in 2027\, and Collins expected a hike before year-end (investingLive). A 5
 0bp hike or hawkish guidance would hit crypto\, tech and gold. A hold woul
 d set off a relief rally.\n\nKalshi Fed rate odds: https://kalshi.com/fed-
 rate-odds\nInvesting.com: reaction roundup on October CPI: https://www.inv
 esting.com/news/economy-news/reaction-roundup-experts-analysts-weigh-in-on
 -october-cpi-report-5016277\ninvestingLive: Williams sees no 2027 hike: ht
 tps://investinglive.com/central-banks/icymi-three-fed-officials-signal-inf
 lation-fight-continues-williams-sees-no-2027-hike/
CATEGORIES:central bank
URL:https://kalshi.com/fed-rate-odds
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:76eb64214b7d8db5@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART:20261210T083000Z
DTEND:20261210T093000Z
SUMMARY:SNB monetary policy assessment
DESCRIPTION:Quarterly SNB decision\, with the policy rate at 0%.\n\nThe pol
 icy rate has been 0% since June 2025 (financecalendar). In March\, Continu
 um Economics judged market pricing of a possible December 2026 hike overdo
 ne\, and that view may be stale. Watch the wording on CHF strength and FX 
 intervention. A dovish tone or intervention talk weakens the CHF\, and a h
 ike would strengthen it and weigh on Swiss exporters.\n\nSNB media events 
 schedule: https://www.snb.ch/en/ifor/media/id/media_events\nFinancecalenda
 r: SNB rate decision December 2026: https://www.financecalendar.com/event/
 snb-rate-decision-december-2026/
CATEGORIES:central bank
URL:https://www.snb.ch/en/ifor/media/id/media_events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8c55e640f5a908f7@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART:20261210T133000Z
DTEND:20261210T143000Z
SUMMARY:US CPI (November)
DESCRIPTION:November consumer prices\, released the day after the FOMC deci
 sion.\n\nOctober came in hot at +0.4% headline and +0.3% core. Because it 
 lands right after the Fed\, a hot print would test whatever guidance the F
 ed gave and could revive 2027 hike pricing\, which is bearish for crypto a
 nd tech. A soft print would support risk assets.\n\nBLS CPI release schedu
 le: https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/cpi.htm
CATEGORIES:macro
URL:https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/cpi.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:59bfc848f5c9b78e@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261218
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:ECB rate decision
DESCRIPTION:The last ECB decision of 2026\, with new staff projections that
  set the starting point for 2027.\n\nFinancecalendar and Admiral Markets b
 oth list December 17. Sources disagree on the exact time\, and the ECB's o
 wn calendar should confirm it. The projections matter more than the rate. 
 A hawkish turn while the Fed is hiking would support the euro and weigh on
  the CHF cross. A dovish one would widen the US-EU rate gap.\n\nFinancecal
 endar: ECB rate decision December 2026: https://www.financecalendar.com/ev
 ent/ecb-rate-decision-december-2026/\nAdmiral Markets: ECB meeting dates 2
 026: https://admiralmarkets.com/analytics/traders-blog/ecb-meeting-october
 -2026
CATEGORIES:central bank
URL:https://www.financecalendar.com/event/ecb-rate-decision-december-2026/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:db3e3586be695d54@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:Bank of Japan rate decision
DESCRIPTION:A hike from 1.25% to 1.5% is the consensus at the December 17-1
 8 meeting.\n\nThe BoJ held at 1.25% on October 30 by an 8-1 vote\, with Ta
 kata voting for 1.5%. A Bloomberg survey has 83% of economists expecting a
  December hike\, up from 35% a month earlier. Daiwa and MUFG both forecast
  December and then April 2027. A hike strengthens the yen and can force ca
 rry trades to unwind\, which hit crypto and tech in past hikes. A hold wou
 ld weaken the yen.\n\ninvestingLive: Daiwa sees December BoJ hike: https:/
 /investinglive.com/central-banks/daiwa-sees-next-boj-rate-hike-in-december
 -as-ueda-signals-shift-in-policy-phase/\ninvestingLive: Bloomberg survey\,
  most see December hike: https://investinglive.com/central-banks/most-anal
 ysts-now-expect-the-next-boj-rate-hike-in-december-none-see-october-move-b
 loomberg/\nFinancecalendar: BoJ rate decision December 2026: https://www.f
 inancecalendar.com/?p=1260
CATEGORIES:central bank
URL:https://investinglive.com/central-banks/daiwa-sees-next-boj-rate-hike-i
 n-december-as-ueda-signals-shift-in-policy-phase/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:926b93dfd5a1b792@market-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261112T064043Z
DTSTART:20270127T190000Z
DTEND:20270127T200000Z
SUMMARY:FOMC rate decision
DESCRIPTION:The first Fed decision of 2027\, after the January 26-27 meetin
 g.\n\nThe Fed set the date in its tentative 2027 schedule. Williams said i
 n October he saw no case for 2027 hikes (investingLive)\, so guidance here
  shows whether December was the last move. A hawkish surprise would hit cr
 ypto and tech.\n\nFederal Reserve: tentative 2027 FOMC schedule: https://w
 ww.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20250905a.htm\nThri
 ve in Markets: FOMC 2027 dates: https://thriveinmarkets.com/calendar/dates
 /fomc-2027/
CATEGORIES:central bank
URL:https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary2025090
 5a.htm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
